# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module-loading compatibility - applied to EVERY build (ksu-susfs, ksun-only and
# the vanilla control), because these decide whether the phone's PREBUILT vendor
# modules are accepted at all. None of these is a KernelSU / SUSFS option.
#
# HOW THESE WERE FOUND
#   The Wild Kernel on the phone loads all 123 /vendor_dlkm modules (Wi-Fi
#   included) and reports its live config at /proc/config.gz. Dumping it next to
#   ours showed exactly these three differences:
#
#     option                            Wild Kernel (working)   ours (57 refused)
#     CONFIG_MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH  =y                      not set  (=n)
#     CONFIG_MODULE_SCMVERSION          =y                      not set
#     CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_PROTECT         not set, empty list     =y + "protected_module_names_list"
#
#   * BTF: the device's modules carry BTF (CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES=y on
#     both sides). 6.12 REFUSES a module whose BTF does not match the running
#     kernel's type IDs unless this option is on, and only the modules touching
#     types whose IDs moved are hit - which is why it looked like a random
#     subset (cfg80211 refused, so bcmdhd4390 went down with it, and so on).
#   * SIG_PROTECT: makes signature verification MANDATORY for a list of
#     protected modules. Our build signs with its own generated key while every
#     module on the phone is Google-signed, so the protected ones get rejected.
#     The known-good Wild Kernel does not enable it.
#   * SCMVERSION: adds the SCM token to the MODULE vermagic. With
#     CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y that token is skipped when vermagic is compared, so
#     this is belt-and-braces: it is here to match a kernel proven to load these
#     modules. It does not affect UTS_RELEASE / /proc/version.
#
# PROVEN NOT TO BE A KERNELSU/SUSFS VERSION QUESTION (checked at source level):
#   the SUSFS kernel patch touches 24 files, all implementations, ZERO headers,
#   and pin -> tip adds no declaration at all; the entire KernelSU-Next delta
#   between the pinned commit and dev-susfs lives inside its own kernel/ tree.
#   Neither can move a symbol CRC, so the dev tips remain a free choice - what
#   they change is the userspace handshake, not module compatibility.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH=y
CONFIG_MODULE_SCMVERSION=y
# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_PROTECT is not set
